course: dictionary
lesson: 5396
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning is right. Kola is one of these words. It can be a tree, a nut from that tree, or the name of a place.
explain: Look for clues. A capital letter in the middle of a sentence often means a name. In «The deepest hole ever drilled, the Kola Superdeep Borehole in Russia, reached about 12 km», Kola starts with a capital letter and is part of a name, so it is the place, not the nut.
explain: Now read this: «Ama chewed a kola nut as a sign of welcome.» Chewed and nut are the clues. A kola nut is a seed that people chew, so kola here means the nut. Always try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning. This is called having several meanings.
fact: «Kola» can mean a tree from West Africa, the seed of that tree (the kola nut), or a place name.
fact: The kola nut contains caffeine, and it was once used to flavour cola drinks.
fact: The Kola Peninsula is a large piece of land in the far north-west of Russia, near Finland and Norway.
fact: In parts of West Africa, kola nuts are shared as a sign of welcome and friendship.
exercise: «The Kola Superdeep Borehole in Russia reached about 12 km.» What does Kola mean here? | *A place name, in Russia | A cola drink | A nut that people chew | A tree from West Africa
exercise: In parts of West Africa, people share a kola nut to show welcome. What is a kola nut? | A type of caffeine | *The seed of the kola tree, which people chew | A cola drink | A tree that grows in Russia
exercise: Which meaning of kola is a place? | Cola drinks | The kola nut | The kola tree | *The Kola Peninsula
test: Why does caffeine in a kola nut matter when it is used to flavour a drink? | Because it is a place name | Because it is from Russia | It makes the nut turn into a drink | *Because a kola nut contains caffeine
test: «The Kola Peninsula lies near Finland and Norway.» Where is the Kola Peninsula? | In the middle of Finland | *In the far north-west of Russia | On a cola bottle | In West Africa
exam: Read this: «Kola grows as a tall tree in West Africa, and its nuts were once used to flavour drinks.» Which meaning of kola is used here? | The place name in Russia | *The tree | A cola drink | A welcome gift from Finland
